# Minimal Einstein-summation Install

## macOS Build Check With Docker

macOS cannot compile or run CUDA/cuTENSOR code directly. Use the provided
Dockerfile to build inside a Linux CUDA 11.4 image with cuTENSOR 1.3.3.2 and
mount this project as a shared folder:

```bash
docker build -t einsum-cuda-builder .
docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/workspace" einsum-cuda-builder make
```

The Dockerfile defaults to `linux/amd64` because NVIDIA's cuTENSOR 1.3.3.2
redist archive used here is the x86_64 package. On Apple Silicon, Docker may
print a host-platform warning before building or running the container.

The output executable is written into the mounted project folder:

```text
./einsum
```

To open a shell in the same build environment:

```bash
docker run --rm -it -v "$PWD:/workspace" einsum-cuda-builder bash
```

Runtime execution still requires a Linux host with an NVIDIA GPU, driver, and
NVIDIA Container Toolkit:

```bash
docker run --rm --gpus all -it -v "$PWD:/workspace" einsum-cuda-builder ./einsum
```

## Native Linux Requirements

Build on Linux with:

```text
CUDA Toolkit 11.x
cuTENSOR 1.3.3
```

The Makefile expects the cuTENSOR archive layout under `/opt/cutensor` by
default. Install cuTENSOR 1.3.3.2 from NVIDIA's redist archive:

```bash
wget https://developer.download.nvidia.com/compute/cutensor/redist/libcutensor/linux-x86_64/libcutensor-linux-x86_64-1.3.3.2-archive.tar.xz
sudo mkdir -p /opt
sudo tar -xJf libcutensor-linux-x86_64-1.3.3.2-archive.tar.xz -C /opt
sudo mv /opt/libcutensor-linux-x86_64-1.3.3.2-archive /opt/cutensor
export CUTENSOR_HOME=/opt/cutensor
export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/opt/cutensor/lib/11:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH
```

Install a CUDA 11 toolkit separately. For Ubuntu 20.04 with NVIDIA's CUDA apt
repository enabled, one compatible option is:

```bash
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y cuda-toolkit-11-4
```

## Build

The Makefile assumes:

```text
CUDA_HOME=/usr/local/cuda
CUTENSOR_HOME=/opt/cutensor
```

Build:

```bash
make
```

Override paths when libraries are installed elsewhere:

```bash
make CUDA_HOME=/path/to/cuda CUTENSOR_HOME=/path/to/cutensor
```

## Run

```bash
./einsum
```

Starter commands:

```text
A = load data/A.txt
B = load data/B.txt
C = einsum ij,jk->ik A B
show C
show C --output=data/C.bin
```

Use `help` inside the prompt for all supported commands and einsum examples.
